From: xtandard-image
Subject: [PATCH] The interleaved alpha plane uses the image's lookup tables

Found by fuzzing (Go FuzzJXR, confirmed with ASan): ImageStrDecDecode
rebuilt the shared offset tables from the interleaved alpha plane's header;
a plane claiming a subsampled colour format halved them and the image then
read past their end. Both planes share m_Dparam and, in a valid file, the
same geometry: build the tables once, from the image.
---
--- a/image/decode/strdec.c
+++ b/image/decode/strdec.c
@@ -3463,14 +3463,16 @@
     {
         if(initLookupTables(pSC) != ICERR_OK)
             return ICERR_ERROR;
-        if (pNextSC && initLookupTables(pNextSC) != ICERR_OK)
-            return ICERR_ERROR;
+        // The interleaved alpha plane shares m_Dparam, so the image's tables
+        // serve it; rebuilding them from its own (corrupt) plane header made
+        // them shorter than the image and the image read past them.
     }
 #else
     if(initLookupTables(pSC) != ICERR_OK)
         return ICERR_ERROR;
-    if (pNextSC && initLookupTables(pNextSC) != ICERR_OK)
-        return ICERR_ERROR;
+    // The interleaved alpha plane shares m_Dparam, so the image's tables
+    // serve it; rebuilding them from its own (corrupt) plane header made
+    // them shorter than the image and the image read past them.
 #endif // REENTRANT_MODE
 
 #ifndef REENTRANT_MODE
